---
description: Keep secrets on the server; never put API keys in the Expo app.
globs: mobile/**,server/**
alwaysApply: true
---

# Secrets stay on the server

- Put keys in `.env` (git-ignored). Never hardcode ElevenLabs, Grok, Mapbox, or Supabase keys.
- The phone app talks to `/api` through `mobile/src/api.js`. Base URL is `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` only (`mobile/.env`, or injected by `npm run tunnel` when unset).
- Read helpers in `api.js` return `null` on network failure so screens can fall back to sample data.
- A failed online mutation must never become a successful local claim. With no API URL configured (offline play, before the deploy), territory rules run locally in demo mode and on real walks.
- Do not add Nessie or other bank APIs. Eggs are earned by walking.
- Supabase turf writes use revision-checked RPCs from `server/supabase/schema.sql`; never replace them with a read followed by a blind upsert.
